{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_gq3v4wrwye7l3xsog6xjgczo2n34gfchw32n2hmlme4krku2uieq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **85 tests, ~10M differential cases, all passing under every configuration.**\n\n## What was found and fixed\n\n**One real bug** — NaN payload/sign propagation. The C is built unoptimised, so every float expression is one x86 SSE instruction with a *fixed* destination register, and `addss dst, src` returns `quiet(dst)` if `dst` is NaN else `quiet(src)`. Rust's plain `+`/`*` let LLVM commute operands, so signalling/quiet NaNs came back with the wrong payload. Reproducible examples:\n\n| call | C | Rust (before) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `c2Dot((178.35, -qNaN), (sNaN 0x7f818097, 0))` | `ffc00000` | `7fc18097` |\n| `c2Add((qNaN,0), (-qNaN,32))` | `ffc00000` | `7fc00000` |\n| `c2Mulrv({12,-0}, (sNaN,sNaN)).y` | `7fd62c79` | `7fdd66ad` |\n\nFixed by decoding the operand order for all 35 arithmetic sites from `objdump -d` of the C `.so` and adding `addss`/`subss`/`mulss`/`divss`/`quiet` helpers in `src/lib.rs` that reproduce x86 dst/src NaN selection exactly. `sqrt`, `xorps` negation, and all `comiss` ternaries already matched.\n\n**Three ERRORS.md rows were wrong on first pass** and I corrected them against measured C behaviour rather than assuming the Rust was at fault:\n- **`cache->count >= 4`**: the C **segfaults** (exit 139) — `int saveA[3]` is written at index 3 and `verts[4]` runs past `c2Simplex::d`. Unbounded stack corruption, no result to match. Now tested out-of-process (asserts the C dies, the Rust returns deterministically) plus a `count = 1..3` control that must match byte-for-byte.\n- **Out-of-range `C2_TYPE` into `c2GJK`**: `c2MakeProxy` writes nothing, so the C reads an uninitialised `c2Proxy`; its garbage `count` drives `c2Support`'s loop and the C either returns `+inf` or segfaults. Also tested out-of-process.\n- **`c23` with `area == 0`**: the final `else` (`count=3, div=0`) is unreachable — all three `?ABC <= 0` tests hold so an earlier collapse/edge branch always wins. Asserted as an observed invariant.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — 38/38, symbol diff empty both ways; all Rust imports are libc/runtime; C's only import is `sqrtf`.\n- `ERRORS.md` — 62 rows, each with a passing differential test (29 tests).\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 95 rows, all `[x]`, each driven with randomized inputs at a fixed seed.\n- `tests/` — `common/mod.rs` harness (both `.so`s via `libloading`, bit-exact comparators, SplitMix64), `phase_b_{leaf,simplex,gjk,predicates}`, `phase_c_errors`, `layout` (probes the C's real struct offsets), `symbols`, `fuzz_differential` (7.6M arbitrary-bit-pattern cases).\n- `run_all_configs.sh` — enumerates features from `Cargo.toml` and sweeps every subset × release/debug. No features are declared, so the meaningful axis is the codegen profile; both pass.\n\nNo driver binary exists (`CMakeLists.txt` builds only `SHARED`, crate is `cdylib`), so `driver_equivalent_stdout_compare` formats `aabb()` over a 61×61 grid from both `.so`s and compares 151,646 bytes of text — identical. `c_src/` unmodified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1068,"cache_read_input_tokens":294004,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1068,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36197e55-e2d7-4aeb-bb1e-b807856a26ea","uuid":"84971968-6ce1-4a17-9a0c-7cfd6489d8ed","timestamp":"2026-09-05T06:07:41.503Z"}
